WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.950
Step 1. Open the public workspace and load the starter library
or select an existing script.

00:03.000 --> 00:05.950
Step 2. Choose User to view, Editor to edit scripts,
or Administrator to also create scripts and shared taxonomy.

00:06.000 --> 00:08.950
Step 3. Select the interface language and work
in public or restricted script mode.

00:09.000 --> 00:11.950
Step 4. Download or upload the collection as JSON.
The recipient uploads the file as their local workspace.

00:12.000 --> 00:14.950
Step 5. Explore scenes and modi operandi.
Link icons show where taxonomy items are used.

00:15.000 --> 00:17.950
Step 6. Share a public script by link or export
JSON, Word, or an SVG/PNG barrier model.

00:18.000 --> 00:20.950
Step 7. Select Edit Script to change scenes,
modi operandi, and activities.

00:21.000 --> 00:23.950
Step 8. Open Generate with LLM and describe
the language, topic, region, detail level, and sources.

00:24.000 --> 00:26.950
Step 9. Review the generated prompt
and copy it to an LLM of your choice.

00:27.000 --> 00:29.950
Step 10. Paste only the JSON response back into PAX.
PAX processes and validates it locally.

00:30.000 --> 00:36.000
Step 11. Review scenes, taxonomy, and sources.
Import only after a substantive review.

00:36.000 --> 00:39.950
Step 12. Compare concrete case observations.
Review matched evidence and any unexplained facts.

00:40.000 --> 00:44.000
Step 13. Reconstruct parts of a public script.
Compare your interpretation without treating differences as automatically wrong.
